@startuml fig_derived_vs_history
!include _style.puml
' Book figure — the two stored branches of one canonical fact.
' Form: structure. Evidence status: conceptual illustration; asserts no rate.
title one canonical fact feeds a derived current-state copy or a retained history
top to bottom direction
skinparam nodesep 16
skinparam ranksep 26

rectangle "canonical Donation" as B0 <<authoritative>>
rectangle "derived current-state copy\nrollup · rolldown\nrebuildable from the facts" as B1 <<derived>>
rectangle "retained historical facts\nevent / ledger\nnot rebuildable once destroyed" as B2 <<authoritative>>

B0 --> B1 : derived
B0 --> B2 : retained

note right of B1
  answers from current state;
  owes its maintainer a
  correctness contract
end note
note right of B2
  preserves information
  that would otherwise
  disappear
end note
@enduml
